{
  "about": "Cases of storm_ui_pack_check (tools/pack_check.cpp): the real UI pack drawn with the real screen and HUD adapters. Every models/*.json that is an interface model and is not used below is a case of its own. A case feeds `states` (channel=file, in order) and then its `interface`, then `answer` (the model the game answers a request of the opened screen with: a shop asks for its selected row's deal); `covers` names the screens it draws that its interface does not (channel screens). `taps` = element ids tapped (a real touch on the drawn element, in order) after all that: a HUD state that a tap opens (the abilities row, the ammunition fan, the raised spyglass). Every ported screen (screens/registry.cpp) must be covered by a case or listed in `uncovered` with the reason. `flows`: taps the game answers in steps, replayed with its real answers one game frame at a time (tools/pack_check.cpp RunFlow): what the last tap shows must have no transient frame (the flicker check, src/action_trace.h); with `predicted` the tap must be one its screen predicts, its result drawn in the tap's own frame although the game answers `wait` frames later (the latency rule). `flicker`: exemptions [{case, tap, reason}] for a transient frame the crawl finds in a tap that needs no game; each needs its reason.",
